language 0.1.0
module file
  means
    Named containers of data offered by a file system, the way they are
    addressed, and the manner in which they are gathered for processing.

entity file-system : thing
  means
    file system: a named hierarchy of containers within which data is
    addressed by paths.

entity file : thing
  means
    file: a named container of data, retained beyond the execution that
    wrote it.

entity directory : thing
  means
    directory: a container holding files and other directories and giving
    them their place in a hierarchy.

entity path : thing
  means
    path: the sequence of names by which a file or a directory is addressed
    within a file system.

entity file-name : thing
  means
    file name: the name distinguishing a file among the others of one
    directory.

entity extension : thing
  means
    extension: the trailing part of a file name by which the kind of its
    content is declared.

entity file-set : thing
  means
    file set: the files gathered for one processing, regardless of the
    directories they were found in.
